# BettaPay CODEOWNERS
#
# GitHub requests a review from the matched owner(s) automatically when a
# pull request touches these paths. That's advisory by default; enabling
# "Require review from Code Owners" under branch protection for `main`
# makes it a hard merge gate. See CONTRIBUTING.md's "Code Ownership"
# section for why these specific paths are gated and how enforcement
# works.
#
# GitHub CODEOWNERS syntax: later, more specific patterns override earlier
# ones for a given path, so keep broad defaults first and narrow
# exceptions below them. Owners must be GitHub usernames (`@user`) or
# teams (`@org/team`) with write access to this repository.

# Architecture Decision Records. These record *why* a cross-cutting
# tradeoff was made a certain way (see adr/003-ttl-value-selection.md for
# an example) — changing an accepted decision, or its rationale, needs
# sign-off from someone who can weigh the original tradeoff, not just a
# style/wording review.
/adr/                               @therealjhay

# Shared cross-contract constants (BPS_DENOMINATOR, TTL thresholds/bumps,
# recovery delay, ...). A change here silently affects both contracts at
# once, so it needs the same reviewer who understands the ADRs that
# justify these specific values.
/bettapay_common/src/constants.rs   @therealjhay

# Deployment, build, and CI-invoked tooling. Breaking these breaks every
# contributor's local `make all` and the CI gate itself.
/scripts/                           @therealjhay
/Makefile                           @therealjhay
/.github/workflows/                 @therealjhay
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @therealjhay

